IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`

-- g1-art2-entity.l4: Article 2(1) to (6) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: the kinds of entity, the Minister's power to add kinds, "Jersey entity",
-- and the meanings of "constitution", "constitutional Law" and "purpose" by kind of entity.
-- Source: the consolidated text "from 2 October 2026", INPUTS/charities-jersey-law-2014-2026-10-02.txt; every quotation is a slice of that file (src:N is line N).
--
-- How the module is built.
--   * The raw facts about a body are the record `Facts about the body under Article 2`: one witness-level fact per sub-paragraph, as a person looking at the body could state it.
--     Whether a body is a company, a foundation, a trust or an NPO is the status the body has under ANOTHER enactment (out of scope), so it is an input.
--   * Each sub-paragraph of Article 2(1) is a rule of its own over those facts; `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` lists the sub-paragraphs the body falls within,
--     in the Law's order. A body can be in more than one (Article 8(3)(a)(i): a company that is the sole trustee is in (a) and (f)), so the answer is a LIST.
--   * Sub-paragraph (ba) was inserted by the Charities (Entities) Law (Jersey) Amendment Order 2025 (R&O.56/2025), made 9 October 2025 under Article 2(2) and in force 7 days after,
--     on 16 October 2025. It is in the text of 16 October 2025 and the text of 2 October 2026, and not in any earlier text. The text is the vintage, an input (Vintages are inputs).
--     No text before 1 January 2019 is among the sources, so the first vintage refuses. The Table of Legislation History lists no amendment of Article 2(1) but R&O.56/2025
--     (endnote [2]), which suggests the other ten sub-paragraphs read the same in every text from 1 January 2019; that reading is taken here, and is not shown by a consolidated text.
--   * Four forks of the group live here: F1.1 (does "(a) to (h)" reach (ba)), F1.3 (the constitutional Law of (g) and (h)), F1.4 (a body in more than one kind),
--     F1.6 (the reach of "in relation to Jersey" in (e)) and F1.8 (does (g) overlap (c), (d), (f)). Each public decision that depends on one takes `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`.

§ `Part 1 — Interpretation`

§§ `2 Definition of entity and related terms`

-- src:47 | 2 Definition of entity and related terms
-- src:48 | (1) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, “entity” means –
-- The lead-in is "unless the context otherwise requires"; no place was found in Article 2(1) where the context displaces the list.

§§§ `2(1) the facts about a body, and the kinds of entity`

-- The raw facts about a body, one field per question the sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1), the definition of a Jersey entity in Article 2(3), and the lookups of Article 2(5) ask.
-- Each field starts at the complement ("the body is ..." supplies the verb), and most are the status of the body under another enactment, so they are inputs.
DECLARE `Facts about the body under Article 2` HAS
    `the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(a): the body is the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust (a trust over which the court has jurisdiction under Article 5 of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984)
    `the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(b): the body is the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis (one created under, or extended the benefits of, the Loi of 1862)
    `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the body is a body corporate; read by Article 2(1)(ba) and (e)
    `an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(ba)(i): the body is an NPO as that Law defines it
    `established under the law of Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(ba)(ii): the body is established under the law of Jersey
    `an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(c): the body is an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862
    `a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(d): the body is a foundation incorporated under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009
    `established by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(e)(i): the body corporate was established by an enactment
    `established by Act of the States` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(e)(ii): the body corporate was established by Act of the States
    `established by Royal Charter` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(e)(iii): the body corporate was established by Royal Charter
    `established in relation to Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the enactment, Act of the States or Royal Charter that established the body corporate was made in relation to Jersey; read by Article 2(1)(e) (fork F1.6)
    `the Law by which the body corporate was established` IS A MAYBE STRING
        @desc Article 2(5)(e): the name of the Law by which the body corporate was incorporated (but not under which it was), if it was established by a Law; NOTHING if it was established by Act of the States, by Royal Charter or by another enactment that is not a Law
    `a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(f): the body is a company registered under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991, or an existing company within the meaning of that Law
    `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(g): the body is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991; read as written, this is also true of a foundation and of an incorporated 1862 association
    `incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(h): the body is incorporated under, but not by, such an Act or Order in Council
    `the enactment under which the body was incorporated` IS A MAYBE STRING
        @desc The name of the enactment under which a body within (g) or (h) was incorporated, if known; read only under the second reading of fork F1.3
    `the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(i): the body is the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons
    `a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the unincorporated body is a partnership, which Article 2(1)(i) leaves out
    `the kinds mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to` IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
        @desc Article 2(1)(j): the sub-paragraphs among (a) to (h) (including the inserted (ba), when it is in the text) that the body is substantially similar to; empty if none. Which is similar is a judgement and is an input
    `established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(1)(j): the body is established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey
    `the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(3)(b)(i): for an unincorporated body, the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey
    `the sub-paragraphs added by Order within which the body falls` IS A LIST OF STRING
        @desc Article 2(2): the labels of the sub-paragraphs that an Order has added to Article 2(1) and within which the body falls; empty if none. The content of an Order is an input (R&O.56/2025, which added (ba), is handled by the text of the Law, not by this list)
    governors IS A LIST OF Governor
        @desc Article 2(3)(b)(ii): the governors of the body, each a person who is a governor under Article 2(7)

-- Reading the Law's own order: (a), (b), (ba), (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (h), (i), (j), and then whatever an Order adds.

-- src:49 | (a) the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust;
@ref Article 2(1)(a) (src:49)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(a) the body is the trustees of a trust` facts MEANS
    facts's `the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust`

-- src:50 | (b) without prejudice to the generality of sub-paragraph (a), the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis;
-- "Without prejudice to the generality of sub-paragraph (a)": (b) adds to (a) and takes nothing from it. Whether a court-approved fidéicommis is also a trust within Article 1 is a fact about the body
-- (an input): a body for which both facts are given is in both (a) and (b).
@ref Article 2(1)(b) (src:50)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(b) the body is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` facts MEANS
    facts's `the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`

-- src:55 | (c) an incorporated 1862 association;
@ref Article 2(1)(c) (src:55)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(c) the body is an incorporated 1862 association` facts MEANS
    facts's `an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862`

-- src:56 | (d) a foundation;
@ref Article 2(1)(d) (src:56)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(d) the body is a foundation` facts MEANS
    facts's `a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009`

-- src:57 | (e) a body corporate established –
-- src:58 | (i) by an enactment,
-- src:59 | (ii) by Act of the States, or
-- src:60 | (iii) by Royal Charter, in relation to Jersey;
-- Fork F1.6: the comma after "Royal Charter" and the position of "in relation to Jersey" leave two readings. Reading A (taken): the words qualify the Royal Charter only, so a body corporate
-- established by an enactment or by Act of the States is within (e) whatever it is in relation to; reading B: they qualify each of (i) to (iii).
@ref Article 2(1)(e)(i) (src:57-58)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(e)(i) the body corporate is established by an enactment` facts MEANS
        facts's `a body corporate`
    AND facts's `established by an enactment`

@ref Article 2(1)(e)(ii) (src:57, src:59)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(e)(ii) the body corporate is established by Act of the States` facts MEANS
        facts's `a body corporate`
    AND facts's `established by Act of the States`

@ref Article 2(1)(e)(iii) (src:57, src:60)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(e)(iii) the body corporate is established by Royal Charter` facts MEANS
        facts's `a body corporate`
    AND facts's `established by Royal Charter`

@ref Article 2(1)(e) (src:57-60)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(e) reading A: in relation to Jersey qualifies the Royal Charter only` facts MEANS
        `Art 2(1)(e)(i) the body corporate is established by an enactment` facts
    OR  `Art 2(1)(e)(ii) the body corporate is established by Act of the States` facts
    OR  (    `Art 2(1)(e)(iii) the body corporate is established by Royal Charter` facts
         AND facts's `established in relation to Jersey`)

@ref Article 2(1)(e) (src:57-60)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(e) reading B: in relation to Jersey qualifies each of (i), (ii) and (iii)` facts MEANS
        (    `Art 2(1)(e)(i) the body corporate is established by an enactment` facts
         OR  `Art 2(1)(e)(ii) the body corporate is established by Act of the States` facts
         OR  `Art 2(1)(e)(iii) the body corporate is established by Royal Charter` facts)
    AND facts's `established in relation to Jersey`

@ref Article 2(1)(e) (src:57-60)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(e) the body is a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` interp facts MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `reach of in relation to Jersey`
    WHEN `only the Royal Charter in sub-paragraph (iii)` THEN `Art 2(1)(e) reading A: in relation to Jersey qualifies the Royal Charter only` facts
    WHEN `each of sub-paragraphs (i), (ii) and (iii)` THEN `Art 2(1)(e) reading B: in relation to Jersey qualifies each of (i), (ii) and (iii)` facts

-- src:61 | (f) a company;
@ref Article 2(1)(f) (src:61)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(f) the body is a company` facts MEANS
    facts's `a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`

-- src:62 | (g) a body incorporated under, but not by, any enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- Fork F1.8: read as written, "any enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991" includes the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009 and the Loi of 1862, so a foundation is within (d) and (g)
-- and an incorporated 1862 association within (c) and (g). Article 8(3)(a)(i) asks for "the sub-paragraph" within which the entity falls, which suggests the drafter meant them to be exclusive.
@ref Article 2(1)(g) (src:62)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(g) the body is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies Law` interp facts MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `overlap of sub-paragraph (g)`
    WHEN `as written, so a foundation or an incorporated 1862 association is also within (g)` THEN
        facts's `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
    WHEN `(g) is the residue, so a body within (c), (d) or (f) is not also within (g)` THEN
            facts's `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
        AND NOT `Art 2(1)(c) the body is an incorporated 1862 association` facts
        AND NOT `Art 2(1)(d) the body is a foundation` facts
        AND NOT `Art 2(1)(f) the body is a company` facts

-- src:63 | (h) a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey;
@ref Article 2(1)(h) (src:63)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(h) the body is incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council` facts MEANS
    facts's `incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey`

-- src:51 | (ba) a body corporate that –
-- src:52 | (i) is an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008;
-- src:53 | (ii) is established under the law of Jersey; and
-- src:54 | (iii) does not fall within any of sub-paragraphs (c) to (h);
-- Endnote [2]: Article 2(1) was amended by R&O.56/2025, which inserted (ba) "after paragraph (1)(b)" under the power in Article 2(2). The Order was made on 9 October 2025 and "comes into force
-- 7 days after it is made": 16 October 2025 (the Table of Legislation History gives the same day). (ba) is in the text of 16 October 2025 and the text of 2 October 2026 and in no earlier text.
-- The counting of "7 days after it is made" belongs to the vintage resolver (fork F7.2): this module takes the text as an input.
@ref Article 2(1)(ba) (src:51-54)
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(ba) is part of the text of` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `before the first consolidated version` THEN `Art 1 no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2019` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 31 May 2019` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 16 December 2019` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2020` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 2 March 2021` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 12 April 2023` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 27 February 2024` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 16 October 2025` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text of 2 October 2026` THEN TRUE

-- Sub-paragraphs (c) to (h): the test in (ba)(iii).
@ref Article 2(1)(ba)(iii) (src:54)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(ba)(iii) the body falls within one of sub-paragraphs (c) to (h)` interp facts MEANS
        `Art 2(1)(c) the body is an incorporated 1862 association` facts
    OR  `Art 2(1)(d) the body is a foundation` facts
    OR  `Art 2(1)(e) the body is a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` interp facts
    OR  `Art 2(1)(f) the body is a company` facts
    OR  `Art 2(1)(g) the body is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies Law` interp facts
    OR  `Art 2(1)(h) the body is incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council` facts

@ref Article 2(1)(ba) (src:51-54)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(ba) the body is a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` interp `the vintage of the text` facts MEANS
        `Art 2(1)(ba) is part of the text of` `the vintage of the text`
    AND facts's `a body corporate`
    AND "(i)" ... facts's `an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`
    AND "(ii)" ... facts's `established under the law of Jersey`
    AND "(iii)" ... NOT `Art 2(1)(ba)(iii) the body falls within one of sub-paragraphs (c) to (h)` interp facts

-- src:64 | (i) the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons, other than a partnership and other than the trustees of a trust;
@ref Article 2(1)(i) (src:64)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(i) the body is an unincorporated body or association of persons` facts MEANS
        facts's `the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons`
    AND NOT facts's `a partnership`
    AND NOT `Art 2(1)(a) the body is the trustees of a trust` facts

-- The sub-paragraphs "(a) to (h)" of Article 2(1), as a list of kinds, for the two places that name the range: (j) below, and Article 2(3)(a).
-- Fork F1.1: (ba) lies between (b) and (c) in the amended list, so by the letters it is inside "(a) to (h)"; R&O.56/2025 amended no other provision.
-- Reading A (taken): the ranges follow the letters, so (ba) is inside whenever it is in the text. Reading B: the ranges are read as of the enactment, so (ba) is outside.
@ref Article 2(1)(j), 2(3)(a) (src:65, src:68)
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`Art 2(1) the sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) with (ba) when it is in the text` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    append (append (LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`)
                   (IF `Art 2(1)(ba) is part of the text of` `the vintage of the text`
                    THEN LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
                    ELSE EMPTY))
           (LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`
               , `a foundation`
               , `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
               , `a company`
               , `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
               , `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`)

@ref Article 2(1)(j), 2(3)(a) (src:65, src:68)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`Art 2(1) the sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) without (ba)` MEANS
    LIST `the trustees of a trust`
       , `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`
       , `an incorporated 1862 association`
       , `a foundation`
       , `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
       , `a company`
       , `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
       , `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`

@ref Article 2(1)(j), 2(3)(a) (src:65, src:68)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`Art 2(1) the sub-paragraphs (a) to (h)` interp `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `ranges and sub-paragraph (ba)`
    WHEN `the ranges follow the letters of the amended list, so (ba) is inside (a) to (h)` THEN
        `Art 2(1) the sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) with (ba) when it is in the text` `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `the ranges are read as of the enactment of the Law, so (ba) is outside (a) to (h)` THEN
        `Art 2(1) the sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) without (ba)`

-- src:65 | (j) an entity that is substantially similar to an entity mentioned in any of sub-paragraphs (a) to (h), but is established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey.[2]
-- "An entity that is substantially similar to an entity": the first "entity" cannot be the defined term, which is what is being defined; it is read as any body. Which kinds the body is
-- substantially similar to is a judgement (an input); the rule asks only whether one of them lies in the range "(a) to (h)", and the range is fork F1.1.
@ref Article 2(1)(j) (src:65)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(j) the body is substantially similar to an entity mentioned in (a) to (h) but established under the law of another jurisdiction` interp `the vintage of the text` facts MEANS
        facts's `established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey`
    AND any (GIVEN kind YIELD elem kind (`Art 2(1) the sub-paragraphs (a) to (h)` interp `the vintage of the text`))
            (facts's `the kinds mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to`)

-- A refusal fires only when something forces it, and a lazy `any` or `elem` can answer before it reaches the one place that refuses. So the list of kinds asks first whether the
-- text of the Law is among the sources at all: TRUE for every text from 1 January 2019, and a refusal for the day before the first consolidated text.
@ref Article 2(1) (src:48)
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1) a text of the Law is among the sources for` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `before the first consolidated version` THEN `Art 1 no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The list. A body that falls within no sub-paragraph is not an entity.
@ref Article 2(1) (src:48-65)
@export The sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (the kinds of entity) within which a body falls, in the Law's order, for a given text of the Law; sub-paragraph (ba) appears only in the texts of 16 October 2025 and later; an empty list means the body is not an entity; it refuses for a day before the first consolidated text of 1 January 2019
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which text of the Law is in force on the day (or instant) in question
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The facts about the body: its status under the other enactments, how it was established, and the rest
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` interp `the vintage of the text` facts MEANS
    IF `Art 2(1) a text of the Law is among the sources for` `the vintage of the text`
    THEN append (map snd (filter fst cases)) added
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        cases MEANS
            LIST (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(a) the body is the trustees of a trust` facts, `the trustees of a trust`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(b) the body is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` facts, `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(ba) the body is a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` interp `the vintage of the text` facts, `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(c) the body is an incorporated 1862 association` facts, `an incorporated 1862 association`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(d) the body is a foundation` facts, `a foundation`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(e) the body is a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` interp facts, `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(f) the body is a company` facts, `a company`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(g) the body is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies Law` interp facts, `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(h) the body is incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council` facts, `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(i) the body is an unincorporated body or association of persons` facts, `an unincorporated body or association of persons`)
               , (PAIR OF `Art 2(1)(j) the body is substantially similar to an entity mentioned in (a) to (h) but established under the law of another jurisdiction` interp `the vintage of the text` facts, `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`)
        added MEANS
            map (GIVEN label YIELD `an entity added by an Order under Article 2(2)` label)
                (facts's `the sub-paragraphs added by Order within which the body falls`)

@ref Article 2(1) (src:48)
@export Whether a body is an entity within Article 2(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, that is, falls within at least one of its sub-paragraphs, for a given text of the Law
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which text of the Law is in force on the day (or instant) in question
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The facts about the body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1) the body is an entity` interp `the vintage of the text` facts MEANS
    NOT null (`Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` interp `the vintage of the text` facts)

§§§ `2(2) the Minister's power to add sub-paragraphs`

-- src:66 | (2) The Minister may by Order add sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1).
-- A power of the Minister: a MAY, typed by who acts and what is done. No period is stated, so there is no WITHIN, and an unexercised power is not a breach (MAY collapses to FULFILLED).
-- The content of an Order (here, the label of the sub-paragraph it adds) is an input; the one Order in the sources is R&O.56/2025, which added (ba), and its effect is in the text of the Law.
-- The Law gives the power to add, not to remove or to change: the only act is to add a sub-paragraph.
DECLARE `Act under Article 2` IS ONE OF
    `make an Order adding a sub-paragraph to Article 2(1)` HAS `label of the added sub-paragraph` IS A STRING

@ref Article 2(2) (src:66)
@export The Minister's power under Article 2(2) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 to add sub-paragraphs to Article 2(1) by Order; the label of the added sub-paragraph is the content of the Order
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 2`
`Art 2(2) the Minister may add a sub-paragraph to Article 2(1)` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `make an Order adding a sub-paragraph to Article 2(1)` label

§§§ `2(3) Jersey entity`

-- src:67 | (3) For the purposes of this Law, an entity is a “Jersey entity” if –
-- src:68 | (a) it falls within any of sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) of paragraph (1); or
@ref Article 2(3)(a) (src:67-68)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3)(a) the body falls within any of sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) of Article 2(1)` interp `the vintage of the text` facts MEANS
    any (GIVEN kind YIELD elem kind (`Art 2(1) the sub-paragraphs (a) to (h)` interp `the vintage of the text`))
        (`Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` interp `the vintage of the text` facts)

-- src:69 | (b) it is an unincorporated body or association of persons falling within paragraph (1)(i), in respect of which –
-- src:70 | (i) the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting the body or association, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey, and
-- src:71 | (ii) at least one governor is a natural person resident in Jersey, or is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of sub-paragraph (a).
-- Sub-paragraph (ii) looks through one level: a governor that is itself a Jersey entity counts only "by virtue of sub-paragraph (a)", not by (b). The governor record says which.
@ref Article 2(3)(b)(i) (src:70)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3)(b)(i) the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting the body is the law of Jersey` facts MEANS
    facts's `the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey`

@ref Article 2(3)(b)(ii) (src:71)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3)(b)(ii) at least one governor is a natural person resident in Jersey or a Jersey entity by virtue of sub-paragraph (a)` facts MEANS
    any (GIVEN governor YIELD
                (governor's `is a natural person` AND governor's `is resident in Jersey`)
            OR  governor's `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)`)
        (facts's governors)

@ref Article 2(3)(b) (src:69)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3)(b) the body is an unincorporated body within Article 2(1)(i) governed by the law of Jersey with a qualifying governor` interp `the vintage of the text` facts MEANS
        elem `an unincorporated body or association of persons` (`Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` interp `the vintage of the text` facts)
    AND "(i)" ... `Art 2(3)(b)(i) the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting the body is the law of Jersey` facts
    AND "(ii)" ... `Art 2(3)(b)(ii) at least one governor is a natural person resident in Jersey or a Jersey entity by virtue of sub-paragraph (a)` facts

@ref Article 2(3) (src:67-71)
@export Whether a body is a "Jersey entity" under Article 2(3) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: it falls within sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) of Article 2(1), or it is an unincorporated body governed by the law of Jersey that has a governor who is a natural person resident in Jersey or is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of (a)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork; the field `ranges and sub-paragraph (ba)` decides whether an NPO body corporate counts
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which text of the Law is in force on the day (or instant) in question
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The facts about the body, including its governors
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3) the body is a Jersey entity` interp `the vintage of the text` facts MEANS
        `Art 2(3)(a) the body falls within any of sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) of Article 2(1)` interp `the vintage of the text` facts
    OR  `Art 2(3)(b) the body is an unincorporated body within Article 2(1)(i) governed by the law of Jersey with a qualifying governor` interp `the vintage of the text` facts

-- The entity as the later Parts take it (the shared noun `Entity`): the kinds and the Jersey-entity status are derived here, the governors are the facts' governors, and the name,
-- the standing on the register and the purposes (Article 2(6), as the entity's constitution states them) are inputs.
@ref Article 2(1), 2(3) (src:48, src:67)
@export The entity as Articles 3 to 43 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 take it: its kinds of entity (Article 2(1)) and Jersey-entity status (Article 2(3)) derived from the facts about the body, with its name, standing on the register and purposes as given
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which text of the Law is in force on the day (or instant) in question
      name IS A STRING @desc The entity's name; the registered name once it is registered
      standing IS A `Standing on the register` @desc Where the entity stands on the register on the day in question
      purposes IS A LIST OF Purpose @desc All of the entity's purposes (Article 2(6))
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The facts about the body
GIVETH AN Entity
`Art 2 the body as an entity` interp `the vintage of the text` name standing purposes facts MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS name
        `standing on the register` IS standing
        `kinds of entity` IS `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` interp `the vintage of the text` facts
        `is a Jersey entity` IS `Art 2(3) the body is a Jersey entity` interp `the vintage of the text` facts
        governors IS facts's governors
        purposes IS purposes

§§§ `2(4) constitution`

-- src:72 | (4) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, “constitution” in relation to an entity means –
-- The seven cases, with what each says the constitution consists of. The documents themselves are an input wherever another Article reads them; this rule says what they are.
-- Article 2(4) is a list of cases ("in the case of a trust ...", "in the case of a company ..."). A body can be in more than one (Article 8(3)(a)(i)): fork F1.4 asks whether every case that
-- applies counts (reading A, taken) or only the first, in the order (a) to (g) (reading B). Paragraph (g) is "in any other case": it applies when none of (a) to (f) does.
-- src:73 | (a) in the case of a trust the terms of the trust;
@ref Article 2(4)(a) (src:73)
`Art 2(4)(a) the constitution of a trust` MEANS "the terms of the trust"

-- src:74 | (b) in the case of a court-approved fidéicommis, the minute of the contract annexed to the application to the court for the creation of the fidéicommis, any other documents so annexed, and any authorisation granted by the court under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862 in respect of the fidéicommis;
@ref Article 2(4)(b) (src:74)
`Art 2(4)(b) the constitution of a court-approved fidéicommis` MEANS
    "the minute of the contract annexed to the application to the court for the creation of the fidéicommis, any other documents so annexed, and any authorisation granted by the court under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862 in respect of the fidéicommis"

-- src:75 | (c) in the case of an incorporated 1862 association, the Act of the court incorporating it under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862, and the object and rules approved or modified under that Article;
@ref Article 2(4)(c) (src:75)
`Art 2(4)(c) the constitution of an incorporated 1862 association` MEANS
    "the Act of the court incorporating it under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862, and the object and rules approved or modified under that Article"

-- src:76 | (d) in the case of a foundation, the charter and regulations of the foundation;
@ref Article 2(4)(d) (src:76)
`Art 2(4)(d) the constitution of a foundation` MEANS "the charter and regulations of the foundation"

-- src:77 | (e) in the case of a company, the memorandum and articles of association of the company;
@ref Article 2(4)(e) (src:77)
`Art 2(4)(e) the constitution of a company` MEANS "the memorandum and articles of association of the company"

-- src:78 | (f) in the case of a body corporate falling within paragraph (1)(e), the enactment, Act of the States or Royal Charter that established the body corporate;
@ref Article 2(4)(f) (src:78)
`Art 2(4)(f) the constitution of a body corporate falling within paragraph (1)(e)` MEANS
    "the enactment, Act of the States or Royal Charter that established the body corporate"

-- src:79 | (g) in any other case, any instrument or instruments (in whatever form) that establish the entity or give it any powers.
-- "In whatever form" sits beside Article 11(4)(b), which asks for "a written document": the constitution is wider than a document.
@ref Article 2(4)(g) (src:79)
`Art 2(4)(g) the constitution in any other case` MEANS
    "any instrument or instruments (in whatever form) that establish the entity or give it any powers"

-- A helper for every list of cases below: the results of the cases that apply, under each reading of F1.4. A case is a pair of whether it applies and what it gives, in the order the
-- paragraph lists them. Reading A keeps every result; reading B keeps the first.
@ref Article 2(4) to 2(6); the same helper serves Article 2(7) (src:72-90)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      cases IS A LIST OF PAIR OF BOOLEAN, a
GIVETH A LIST OF a
`Art 2 the results of every case that applies` cases MEANS
    map snd (filter fst cases)

@ref Article 2(4) to 2(6); the same helper serves Article 2(7) (src:72-90)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      cases IS A LIST OF PAIR OF BOOLEAN, a
GIVETH A LIST OF a
`Art 2 the result of only the first case that applies` cases MEANS
    take 1 (map snd (filter fst cases))

@ref Article 2(4) to 2(6); the same helper serves Article 2(7) (src:72-90)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      cases IS A LIST OF PAIR OF BOOLEAN, a
GIVETH A LIST OF a
`Art 2 the results of the cases that apply` interp cases MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `cases for a body in more than one kind`
    WHEN `every case of Article 2(4) to (7) that applies` THEN `Art 2 the results of every case that applies` cases
    WHEN `only the first case of Article 2(4) to (7) that applies, in the order the paragraph lists them` THEN `Art 2 the result of only the first case that applies` cases

@ref Article 2(4) (src:72-79)
@export What the constitution of an entity consists of under Article 2(4) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, for one kind of entity: the terms of the trust, the memorandum and articles of a company, and so on; for a kind that has no case of its own, any instrument that establishes the entity or gives it powers
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraph of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls
GIVETH A STRING
`Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity consists of` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the trustees of a trust` THEN `Art 2(4)(a) the constitution of a trust`
    WHEN `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` THEN `Art 2(4)(b) the constitution of a court-approved fidéicommis`
    WHEN `an incorporated 1862 association` THEN `Art 2(4)(c) the constitution of an incorporated 1862 association`
    WHEN `a foundation` THEN `Art 2(4)(d) the constitution of a foundation`
    WHEN `a company` THEN `Art 2(4)(e) the constitution of a company`
    WHEN `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` THEN `Art 2(4)(f) the constitution of a body corporate falling within paragraph (1)(e)`
    OTHERWISE `Art 2(4)(g) the constitution in any other case`

@ref Article 2(4) (src:72-79)
@export What the constitution of an entity consists of under Article 2(4) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, for an entity that falls within the given kinds (one entry per case that applies, or the first only on the second reading of fork F1.4); an empty list of kinds is not an entity and has no constitution
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork; the field `cases for a body in more than one kind` decides how the cases combine
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls, as the entity's `kinds of entity`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 2(4) the constitution of the entity in all its kinds consists of` interp kinds MEANS
    IF null kinds
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF null specific
         THEN LIST `Art 2(4)(g) the constitution in any other case`
         ELSE specific
    WHERE
        specific MEANS
            `Art 2 the results of the cases that apply` interp
                (LIST (PAIR OF elem `the trustees of a trust` kinds, `Art 2(4)(a) the constitution of a trust`)
                    , (PAIR OF elem `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` kinds, `Art 2(4)(b) the constitution of a court-approved fidéicommis`)
                    , (PAIR OF elem `an incorporated 1862 association` kinds, `Art 2(4)(c) the constitution of an incorporated 1862 association`)
                    , (PAIR OF elem `a foundation` kinds, `Art 2(4)(d) the constitution of a foundation`)
                    , (PAIR OF elem `a company` kinds, `Art 2(4)(e) the constitution of a company`)
                    , (PAIR OF elem `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` kinds, `Art 2(4)(f) the constitution of a body corporate falling within paragraph (1)(e)`))

§§§ `2(5) constitutional Law`

-- src:80 | (5) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, “constitutional Law” means –
-- The five cases (a) to (e) are quoted beside the rules that carry them, below.
-- Trap T6: the definition has a case for five kinds only. It names no Law for a body that is an NPO body corporate (ba), a body incorporated "under, but not by" an enactment (g) or an
-- Act or Order in Council (h), an unincorporated body (i), a foreign entity (j), or an entity an Order adds; and (e) says "by (but not under)", which is the opposite of what (g) and (h) say, and
-- reaches only a body established by a LAW, not one established by Act of the States or by Royal Charter. For every such body the answer is that the definition gives none: an empty list.
-- Fork F1.3: reading A (taken): none for (g) and (h); reading B: the enactment under which the body is incorporated.
DECLARE `Constitutional Law of an entity` IS ONE OF
    `the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984`
    `the Loi of 1862`
    `the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009`
    `the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
    `another Law by which the body corporate was incorporated` HAS `name of the Law` IS A STRING
    `the enactment under which the body was incorporated` HAS `name of the enactment` IS A STRING

-- src:81 | (a) in relation to an entity that is a trust, the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984;
@ref Article 2(5)(a) (src:81)
`Art 2(5)(a) the constitutional Law of a trust` MEANS `the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984`

-- src:82 | (b) in relation to an entity that is a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association, the Loi of 1862;
@ref Article 2(5)(b) (src:82)
`Art 2(5)(b) the constitutional Law of a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association` MEANS `the Loi of 1862`

-- src:83 | (c) in relation to an entity that is a foundation, the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009;
@ref Article 2(5)(c) (src:83)
`Art 2(5)(c) the constitutional Law of a foundation` MEANS `the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009`

-- src:84 | (d) in relation to an entity that is a company, the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991; and
@ref Article 2(5)(d) (src:84)
`Art 2(5)(d) the constitutional Law of a company` MEANS `the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`

-- src:85 | (e) in relation to an entity that is a body incorporated by (but not under) any other Law, that Law.
-- The case applies to a body corporate established by a LAW, and the Law is named by the input; it does not apply to one established by Act of the States or by Royal Charter.
@ref Article 2(5)(e) (src:85)
GIVEN lawName IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Constitutional Law of an entity`
`Art 2(5)(e) the constitutional Law of a body incorporated by (but not under) any other Law` lawName MEANS
    `another Law by which the body corporate was incorporated` lawName

-- Fork F1.3, reading B: for a body within (g) or (h) the enactment under which it is incorporated.
@ref Article 2(5)(e) (src:85)
GIVEN enactmentName IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Constitutional Law of an entity`
`Art 2(5) reading B of F1.3: the constitutional Law of a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment` enactmentName MEANS
    `the enactment under which the body was incorporated` enactmentName

@ref Article 2(5) (src:80-85)
@export The constitutional Laws of an entity under Article 2(5) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, for an entity that falls within the given kinds: the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 for a trust, the Loi of 1862 for a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association, the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009 for a foundation, the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991 for a company, and the Law that incorporated a body corporate established by a Law; an empty list means the definition gives none, which is the answer for several kinds of entity
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork; the fields `cases for a body in more than one kind` and `constitutional Law of (g) and (h)` decide the answer
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls, as the entity's `kinds of entity`
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The facts about the body: the Law that established it, and the enactment under which it was incorporated
GIVETH A LIST OF `Constitutional Law of an entity`
`Art 2(5) the constitutional Laws of the entity are` interp kinds facts MEANS
    `Art 2 the results of the cases that apply` interp (append cases (readingB interp))
    WHERE
        cases MEANS
            LIST (PAIR OF elem `the trustees of a trust` kinds, `Art 2(5)(a) the constitutional Law of a trust`)
               , (PAIR OF (    elem `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` kinds
                           OR  elem `an incorporated 1862 association` kinds), `Art 2(5)(b) the constitutional Law of a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association`)
               , (PAIR OF elem `a foundation` kinds, `Art 2(5)(c) the constitutional Law of a foundation`)
               , (PAIR OF elem `a company` kinds, `Art 2(5)(d) the constitutional Law of a company`)
               , (PAIR OF (    elem `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter` kinds
                           AND isJust (facts's `the Law by which the body corporate was established`))
                          , `Art 2(5)(e) the constitutional Law of a body incorporated by (but not under) any other Law` (fromMaybe "" (facts's `the Law by which the body corporate was established`)))
        readingB reading MEANS
            CONSIDER reading's `constitutional Law of (g) and (h)`
            WHEN `none, because Article 2(5) names no Law for sub-paragraphs (g) and (h)` THEN EMPTY
            WHEN `the enactment under which the body is incorporated` THEN
                LIST (PAIR OF (    (    elem `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` kinds
                                    OR  elem `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council` kinds)
                               AND isJust (facts's `the enactment under which the body was incorporated`))
                         , `Art 2(5) reading B of F1.3: the constitutional Law of a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment` (fromMaybe "" (facts's `the enactment under which the body was incorporated`)))

@ref Article 2(5) (src:80-85)
@export The constitutional Law of one kind of entity under Article 2(5) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, or none (NOTHING) where the definition names none for that kind
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork; the field `constitutional Law of (g) and (h)` decides the answer for sub-paragraphs (g) and (h)
      kind IS A `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraph of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls
      facts IS A `Facts about the body under Article 2` @desc The facts about the body
GIVETH A MAYBE `Constitutional Law of an entity`
`Art 2(5) the constitutional Law of the entity is` interp kind facts MEANS
    listToMaybe (`Art 2(5) the constitutional Laws of the entity are` interp (LIST kind) facts)

§§§ `2(6) purpose`

-- src:86 | (6) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, “purpose” in relation to an entity means –
-- Like Article 2(4), a list of cases, and fork F1.4 decides how the cases combine for a body in more than one kind. The purposes themselves are an input (the shared noun `Purpose`).
-- src:87 | (a) in the case of a trust, the benefit of its beneficiaries or any other purpose mentioned in Article 2(b) of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 by virtue of which the trust exists, as specified in its constitution;
@ref Article 2(6)(a) (src:87)
`Art 2(6)(a) the purpose of a trust` MEANS
    "the benefit of its beneficiaries or any other purpose mentioned in Article 2(b) of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 by virtue of which the trust exists, as specified in its constitution"

-- src:88 | (b) in the case of a court-approved fidéicommis, or of an incorporated 1862 association, the objects for which it was created or incorporated, or that were subsequently authorized under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862;
@ref Article 2(6)(b) (src:88)
`Art 2(6)(b) the purpose of a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association` MEANS
    "the objects for which it was created or incorporated, or that were subsequently authorized under Article 10 of the Loi of 1862"

-- src:89 | (c) in the case of a foundation, the objects specified in its charter or its regulations; or
@ref Article 2(6)(c) (src:89)
`Art 2(6)(c) the purpose of a foundation` MEANS "the objects specified in its charter or its regulations"

-- src:90 | (d) in the case of any other entity, a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination).
@ref Article 2(6)(d) (src:90)
`Art 2(6)(d) the purpose of any other entity` MEANS
    "a purpose to which that entity’s property may lawfully be applied, other than by virtue of an order of a court, in accordance with the powers of the entity as set out in its constitution (including on its winding up or other termination)"

@ref Article 2(6) (src:86-90)
@export What the purpose of an entity means under Article 2(6) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, for one kind of entity: the benefit of the beneficiaries of a trust, the objects of a fidéicommis, an 1862 association or a foundation, and for any other entity a purpose to which its property may lawfully be applied under its constitution
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraph of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls
GIVETH A STRING
`Art 2(6) the purpose of the entity means` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the trustees of a trust` THEN `Art 2(6)(a) the purpose of a trust`
    WHEN `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` THEN `Art 2(6)(b) the purpose of a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association`
    WHEN `an incorporated 1862 association` THEN `Art 2(6)(b) the purpose of a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association`
    WHEN `a foundation` THEN `Art 2(6)(c) the purpose of a foundation`
    OTHERWISE `Art 2(6)(d) the purpose of any other entity`

@ref Article 2(6) (src:86-90)
@export What the purpose of an entity means under Article 2(6) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, for an entity that falls within the given kinds (one entry per case that applies, or the first only on the second reading of fork F1.4); an empty list of kinds is not an entity and has no purpose
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork; the field `cases for a body in more than one kind` decides how the cases combine
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls, as the entity's `kinds of entity`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 2(6) the purposes of the entity in all its kinds mean` interp kinds MEANS
    IF null kinds
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF null specific
         THEN LIST `Art 2(6)(d) the purpose of any other entity`
         ELSE specific
    WHERE
        specific MEANS
            `Art 2 the results of the cases that apply` interp
                (LIST (PAIR OF elem `the trustees of a trust` kinds, `Art 2(6)(a) the purpose of a trust`)
                    , (PAIR OF (    elem `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` kinds
                                OR  elem `an incorporated 1862 association` kinds), `Art 2(6)(b) the purpose of a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association`)
                    , (PAIR OF elem `a foundation` kinds, `Art 2(6)(c) the purpose of a foundation`))
